 <details class="training-more tt-section" id="actions-results"><summary>Training results — what happened to the data</summary>
 <section id="training-reports"><span class="stage-label">YOUR TRAINING RESULTS</span><h2>What happened to the data?</h2><label class="tt-showing">Showing <select id="run-history" aria-label="Choose a training run to show"></select></label><p>Human observations stay in Neptune’s database. The selected computer reads the videos and prepares examples. It sends the model and report back here; your human tags are kept separate.</p><div id="training-result" aria-live="polite"></div><a id="download-report" hidden>Download this report</a><details class="training-more"><summary>Where things are saved</summary><ul><li><strong>Neptune:</strong> human tags, scoring estimates, training reports, model files, prediction results and release status.</li><li><strong>Training computer:</strong> downloaded videos, text readings and extracted video examples, reused for later runs.</li><li><strong>A prediction:</strong> an experimental model result. It does not replace a person’s scouting or become training truth automatically.</li></ul></details></section>
 </details>
 <details class="training-more tt-section"><summary>Saved models</summary>
 <section id="saved-models"><span class="stage-label">MANAGE MODELS</span><h2>Saved models</h2><p>Review models for this game and delete ones you no longer want. Training reports, prediction results, human tags and imported scouting are kept.</p><div id="saved-model-list"></div><p class="training-note">Sizes show the saved model payload, not total training storage. Deleting a model lets MySQL reuse its space; it may not immediately reduce the database file on disk. Helper caches and shared tracking models are separate.</p><p id="saved-model-message" role="status"></p></section>
 </details>
